    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Danny Bernstein",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>escowles: I like the other changes in this PR, but I'm worried about the performance implications of this, esp. for resources with many links to other repository children. Producing the output in order to get its size seems very counter-productive. What is the point of doing a HEAD request if it isn't fast?<br/>\nacoburn: I completely agree with @escowles<br/>\ndbernstein:  @escowles That's an excellent point. I agree with you here. I assumed whoever opened the issue deemed it important to address. Assuming this is still the case, do you have any other ideas about how I might approach this one? Also to consider: once we address the performance concerns related to resources with many links, perhaps your concerns may be less of an issue?<br/>\nacoburn: @dbernstein *personally, I think we should close the issue as \"Won't Fix\". IMO, the only viable alternative is to not include a Content-Length header for HEAD requests on containers. When I looked into this ticket earlier, I did not see a way to do that, as Jersey will (helpfully) add a Content-Length header for you.<br/>\nEven if the performance considerations have been addressed, a HEAD request should, under no circumstances, try to fetch and/or serialize an entire object &#8211; it should only check whether the object exists along with some of the basic LDP types.*</p>",
     "created": "28/Oct/16 9:11 PM",
     "id": "17917",
     "jsdPublic": true,
